/**
 * @mainpage AbacDsp
 *
 * A header-only C++20 DSP library. The core in `src/includes/` has no external
 * dependencies; JUCE appears only in the example plugins.
 *
 * @section conventions Conventions
 *
 * These hold across the whole library, and knowing them makes most individual
 * classes predictable.
 *
 * **Sample rate in the constructor.** Stateful processors take `float
 * sampleRate` on construction and derive their coefficients there. There is no
 * separate prepare step, and no processor reads a global rate.
 *
 * **Block size as a template parameter.** Processing operates on
 * `std::array<float, BlockSize>` rather than a pointer and a length, so the
 * loop bound is a compile-time constant. Block sizes of 8 to 16 samples are
 * typical. AbacDsp::FixedSizeProcessor adapts an arbitrary external block size
 * to a fixed internal one, at exactly one internal block of latency.
 *
 * **No allocation after construction.** Anything on an audio path sizes its
 * storage up front. Where a class does allocate, or blocks, or holds a lock,
 * its documentation says so; treat that as the exception it is.
 *
 * **Wrap padding on interpolated buffers.** Delay lines that interpolate carry
 * a few samples of the buffer duplicated past its end, so a four- or six-point
 * kernel reads across the seam without a bounds test. The padding width is part
 * of each class's contract.
 *
 * **Prime delay lengths.** Delay lines whose lengths share a common factor
 * reinforce each other at that period. Unmodulated chains snap their lengths to
 * distinct primes; see @ref numbers.
 *
 * @section reading Where to start
 *
 * @ref filters and @ref delays hold the primitives most of the rest is built
 * from. @ref reverbs and @ref diffuser show them composed into complete
 * effects. @ref numbers carries the interpolation and conversion routines
 * everything else depends on.
 *
 * The module list has a page per domain, each stating the design decision that
 * domain turns on.
 *
 * @section refs External references
 *
 * Citations throughout point at stable sources, chiefly Julius Smith's online
 * books at CCRMA, the Audio EQ Cookbook, and the DAFx paper archive. They are
 * collected in `WEB-REFERENCES.md` at the repository root and checked with
 * `dev-scripts/dev-check-urls.sh`.
 *
 * @section building Building the documentation
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * dev-scripts/dev-docs.sh
 * @endcode
 *
 * Output lands in `docs/html/index.html`.
 */
